desc:TT-HOTTER Five-Band Linear-Phase Compressor
// @description TT-HOTTER - five-band linear-phase upward/downward compressor with before/after display, target curves, drive and a true-peak ceiling
// @author TimTechlor
// @version 1.0.0
// @link Manual https://timtechlor.de/docs/tt-hotter-manual.html
// @license MIT
// @tags dynamics multiband compressor upward downward linear-phase ott mastering techno
// @provides
//   [nomain] img/tt-ui-options/hotter-front.png
//   [nomain] img/tt-ui-options/hotter-options.png
//   tt-hotter-manual.html
//   img/tt-hotter/tt-hotter-balance.png
//   img/tt-hotter/tt-hotter-scope.png
//   img/tt-hotter/tt-hotter-expert.png
//   img/tt-hotter/tt-hotter-presets.png
// @about
//   # TT-HOTTER
//   Five bands (SUB, LOW, L-MID, MID, HIGH), each with upward and downward compression. The crossovers are linear-phase and freely draggable.
//   Before/after display (SPECTRUM, BALANCE, SCOPE), genre target curves with LEARN and MATCH, post-sum DRIVE, AUTO GAIN and a true-peak CEILING.
//   Latency is 5240 samples (about 109 ms at 48 kHz) plus LOOKAHEAD, reported to REAPER. Ceiling 0 dB means the limiter is off, the delay stays.
//   The twin with three zero-latency bands is TT-HOTT. Not affiliated with any product.
// @changelog
//   1.0.0 - First stable release (Drop 07 of Acid Season), together with TT-HOTT. No sound change from 0.9.10.
//   0.9.10 - First public release (Drop 07 of Acid Season), together with TT-HOTT. Five linear-phase bands, own level-neutral tuning, target curves with LEARN and MATCH, 23 factory presets including seven techno presets.
// GENERIERT von build_hotter.py. Nicht von Hand aendern.

in_pin:In L
in_pin:In R
in_pin:Sidechain L
in_pin:Sidechain R
out_pin:Out L
out_pin:Out R

